CORE
main.c
--32 --unwind 2 --rounds 3 --por --array-rf-bytes --allow-pointer-unsoundness --no-assertions --datarace
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
--
Different members, stored at computed indices by two threads, are different memory locations: no data race. Rebuilding the element used to read every member, and those reads paired with the other thread store. Fails on a binary without the fix.
